  "finding": {
    "id": "HAP-RICHTAP-08",
    "title": "Richtap ioctl 0x5209 can overlap a running threaded IRQ during stop/restart",
    "severity": "high_static",
    "confidence": "high_static_call_paths_and_unshared_locks",
    "stock_observation": "The mode-transition ioctl and the threaded IRQ use different per-device mutexes, or no common mutex in the Richtap FIFO branch. The ioctl performs aw8693x_stop and RTP mode/data programming while the IRQ handler may be executing chip callbacks and FIFO operations.",
    "runtime_reproduced": false,
    "hardware_tested": false,
    "prior_rationale_revised": "The prior mode-transition note said the 0x5209 path needed IRQ service during richtap_rtp_start. Stock Ghidra instead shows a polling callback that reads register 0x3f directly over I2C; the poll itself does not await IRQ service. The existing RTP worker also holds the same shared IRQ mutex while calling richtap_rtp_start."
  },
